    "text": "By Callie Burch ,\n4 hours ago For the better half of her day, Monday through Friday, my mom taught and took care of 30 second graders. She made sure they were fed, taught them how to read and stayed at school late to build a cardboard gingerbread house and staple felt snow to corkboards for the yearly classroom play that she directed herself. She did this for 35 years. Read full article",
